  "summary": "Hey there! I’m Luis Sandoval\n\nA UX/UI Designer & Front-end Developer based in Jacksonville, FL. I’m all about crafting captivating user experiences that leave a lasting impact.\n\nMy journey into the world of design started at The Art Institute, where I delved into Graphic and Web Design from 2008 to 2011. Eager to expand my horizons, I then embarked on a UI/UX Concepts program at UCLA, honing my skills in both design and development from 2012 to 2013.\n\nThroughout my career, I’ve had the pleasure of collaborating with some incredible brands like Adidas, Avianca, and The North Face, just to name a few. These experiences haven’t just added to my skill set—they’ve given me invaluable insights into the ever-evolving landscape of design and development.\n\nCurrently, I’m working as a UX/UI Designer & Front-end Developer, where I get to channel my passion into creating engaging user experiences. From concept to execution, I love bringing ideas to life and seeing the positive impact they have on users.\n\nOutside of work, you’ll often find me spending time with my family, catching waves while surfing, or cruising around on my skateboard. I’m a big fan of technology and love staying up-to-date with the latest trends and innovations.\n\nIn a nutshell, I’m on a mission to blend creativity with functionality, all while enjoying the ride and embracing the endless possibilities of design and technology.",
